Input: {"question": "What is the primary function of Belorechensky?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0274-b7fa11523a04:d00", "start": 0, "end": 138, "text": "Belorechensky District Belorechensky District () is an administrative district (raion), one of the thirty-eight in Krasnodar Krai, Russia."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0274-b7fa11523a04:d00", "start": 139, "end": 219, "text": "As a municipal division, it is incorporated as Belorechensky Municipal District."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0274-b7fa11523a04:d00", "start": 220, "end": 336, "text": "It is located in the southern central part of the krai, but is bordered for the main part by the Republic of Adygea."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0274-b7fa11523a04:d00", "start": 337, "end": 475, "text": "The area of the district is .Its administrative center is the town of Belorechensk (which is not administratively a part of the district)."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0274-b7fa11523a04:d00", "start": 476, "end": 600, "text": "Population: Within the framework of administrative divisions, Belorechensky District is one of the thirty-eight in the krai."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0274-b7fa11523a04:d00", "start": 601, "end": 654, "text": "The town of Belorechensk serves as its administrative"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0274-b7fa11523a04:d01", "start": 0, "end": 96, "text": "Bilorichenska coal mine Bilorichenska coal mine () ranks among the biggest companies of Ukraine."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0274-b7fa11523a04:d01", "start": 97, "end": 178, "text": "It is located in Belorechenskiy, Lutuhynskiy district of Luhansk region, Ukraine."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0274-b7fa11523a04:d01", "start": 179, "end": 228, "text": "The mined coal rank is \"G\" – electric-power coke."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0274-b7fa11523a04:d01", "start": 229, "end": 298, "text": "As of 1 June 2011 reserves of the mine amounted to 11.6 million tons."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0274-b7fa11523a04:d01", "start": 299, "end": 435, "text": "There is an opportunity to cut further spare reserves, following which the mineable reserves could amount up to 70 million tons of coal."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0274-b7fa11523a04:d01", "start": 436, "end": 489, "text": "The design and engineering of the mine began in 1949."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0274-b7fa11523a04:d01", "start": 490, "end": 545, "text": "The project was named Bilorichenska after Belaya river."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0274-b7fa11523a04:d01", "start": 546, "end": 602, "text": "The mine was planned in the area where \"a burning stone\""}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0274-b7fa11523a04:d02", "start": 0, "end": 352, "text": "{ e�� '' �ث $ |�� vg���^�t��w\u00046�b\u0014�\u0006�o � Ħ��4\u0010�\u0006b� @ l\u001a�M\u0003�i 6 Ħ��4\u0010�\u0006b� @ l\u001aql & �D�i 6 ������r * � ) a { vQ2o��k M\u00175ILIz�x�� * erN���� ; ��� ) S # �T� < �O�l\u0018� < �-������Y\\� ' ; Kt��nђ��\u001an $ yT�נi�����-uI-�\u0015 @ q��J��\u0012 % ���|�\u0013A���R�C����뺤t�ŗ_I����d @ ƿ� [ �\u0017�H77p��0y � $ 1��S\u0001�\u0015h��k�N��M�On����\u0015U+u� ] �fy� ����Rt�E��\u0012� � �\b��z����\u0000���Y�¢ƥ��x3��� !"}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0274-b7fa11523a04:d02", "start": 353, "end": 476, "text": "'�����c�����G� � ( yS�٠\u0013�w�M�N\u0014�o����7V�ɋ��\u0005�s���U�v\u00045� ; �b\u0018�� ` ��h\u0012T��7�to��� $ �cj��+ҕ q�JJ� < \u0017�EN�_�J�\u000f Y { �M�Ϥ��� ?"}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0274-b7fa11523a04:d02", "start": 477, "end": 622, "text": "�I�1Mɬ } \u001av < \u0000 ; �aǭ��P : �\u0002��T�\u0017S�\u000e��r��h-B�\\�u�S�W-�3�K'�w�n\u001b+�� : �P ` 6鏞�M���^�6